{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011Cfbox2dNHY1oETJNEUSSj", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The main difference is that **lists are mutable** and **tuples are immutable**.\n\n| | List | Tuple |\n|---|---|---|\n| Syntax | `[1, 2, 3]` | `(1, 2, 3)` or `1, 2, 3` |\n| Mutable | Yes: you can append, remove and reassign items | No: fixed once created |\n| Methods | Many (`append`, `extend`, `insert`, `pop`, `remove`, `sort`, `reverse`, \u2026) | Only `count` and `index` |\n| Hashable | No, so it can't be a dict key or set member | Yes, if all its elements are hashable |\n| Memory/speed | A bit larger, with spare room for growth | Smaller and slightly faster to create |\n| Typical use | A collection of similar items that may grow or change | A fixed group of values, often of different types (a record) |\n\n```python\nnums = [1, 2, 3]\nnums.append(4)        # fine\nnums[0] = 99          # fine\n\npoint = (3, 4)\npoint[0] = 5          # TypeError: 'tuple' object does not support item assignment\n\nlocations = {(40.7, -74.0): \"NYC\"}   # tuple as dict key: OK\nlocations = {[40.7, -74.0]: \"NYC\"}   # TypeError: unhashable type: 'list'\n```\n\n**Things to watch for:**\n- **A one-item tuple needs a trailing comma:** `(5,)` is a tuple, but `(5)` is just the integer 5.\n- **Immutability is shallow:** `t = ([1, 2], 3)` can't be reassigned, but `t[0].append(3)` still works because the inner list is mutable. A tuple like this also isn't hashable.\n- **Tuples make packing and unpacking easy:** `x, y = y, x`, returning several values with `return a, b`, and `namedtuple` or `typing.NamedTuple` for records with named fields.\n\n**Rule of thumb:** use a list for a sequence of items that can change. Use a tuple when the structure is fixed and you want it to stay that way, or when it needs to be hashable."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 7212, "cache_read_input_tokens": 16780, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 7212}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "59a5ca2c-c7f9-4359-9db3-f79976690d7f", "uuid": "a482ec4b-a2a0-4a4b-89e3-d3d552fd547e", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T16:11:24.416Z", "request_id": "req_011Cfbox2Gnn2hYKE4rdVMfs"}
